   Q1, board E's vehicle-entry ideal-diode FET: TI CSD19532Q5B (SLPS414B, byte-identical to ti.com on 2 October 2026), LCSC C473333
     maker's rows: VDS 100 V, VGS +-20 V, ID 17 A (1 in2 2 oz), IDM 400 A, EAS 274 mJ, TJ to 150 C; RDS(on) at VGS 10 V 4 / 4.9 mOhm;
       Vth 2.2 / 2.6 / 3.2 V; VSD at most 1 V; Qg at most 62 nC; RthetaJA at most 50 C/W (1 in2 2 oz; board E's copper an ASSUMPTION)
     normal: 6.15 A (the entry's highest) at RDS(on) 4.9 mOhm x 1.95 (Figure 8 at 150 C, read) = 0.361 W; TJ at most 80.2 C in 62.1 C air (MEETS against 150 C; INFERRED)
       ID 6.15 A against 17 A: MEETS (MAKER); at hot plug the body diode carries the hot swap's limited current for at most 0.131 ms (ENTDLY 110 us plus Qg 62 nC at the controller's 3 mA): 0.804 mJ (INFERRED)
       SOA: Q1 runs fully enhanced or off (the ideal diode regulates only a 20 mV forward drop): no linear dwell to judge
     reverse (REQ-015, -36 V with DC_P back-fed from the raised tracker ceiling through Q7's body diode): VDS 66.15 V against 100 V: MEETS (INFERRED);
       the LM74700-Q1's cathode to anode 66.15 V against 70 V recommended and 75 V absolute, its ANODE -36 V against -65 V: MEETS (MAKER)
       the body diodes: Q1's reverse-biased (it blocks); Q7's forward at DC_P's own milliamps (the back-feed); D10 off (36 V under its 44.4 V
       breakdown); D1 reverse-biased (cathode on DC_P); the input capacitor of E-F1 at -36 V on its 100 V rating
     transients (TEST-PLAN M2 CS101, M3 CS114 and M7 at decision 34's level, as L4-E7R derived them for the solar entry; no surge level is
       ruled, D-16 and CHO-003): CS101 curve 2, 2 V rms, 2.828 V peak: Q1 conducts forward and blocks at most 5.66 V when the controller opens it
       in 0.75 us; at the range's top the input reaches 38.83 V, past the OVLO's 37.78 V minimum: the hot swap may switch off under M2 (an upset
       against M2's line at a 36 V source, not a rating); at curve 2's own boundary, a 28 V source, the top is 30.83 V, 6.95 V under it: MEETS.
       TEST-PLAN M2 states no source voltage, so the finding is a defect at REQ-015's top with two resolutions on the same topology: (i) M2 at
       the source's nominal, stated by TEST-PLAN's owner; (ii) the OVLO moved so its minimum clears 38.83 V and its maximum stays under D10's 44.4 V breakdown
       minimum: R23 from 6.458 k down to 6.346 k with R22 100 k at 1 % (the band re-derived: 37.78 to 42.49 V for R23 6.65 k, as s120 prints); no E96
       value lies inside; E192's 6.42 k at 1 % gives 39.04 to 43.92 V (0.21 V and 0.48 V of margin); with R22 and R23 both 0.1 %: 39.71 to 43.18 V, 0.88 V over the
       CS101 peak and 1.22 V under D10's breakdown minimum at 25 C. D10's breakdown falls 0.1 %/K (typical): 42.4 V at -20 C, under the present
       OVLO maximum already, so steady inputs above it reach D10 when cold; REQ-015 admits steady inputs to 40 V, under it: CONDITIONAL (a
       typical coefficient, not a warranted bound) for REQ-015's
       inputs. SESSION: (ii) at 0.1 % selected (it removes the finding whatever M2's source voltage; register R-94); (i) not taken (a test
       condition is not changed to fit the design); CS114 curve 4, 141 mA rms into E-F1's 1 uF at 10 kHz: at most 3.17 V peak, Q1 blocks
       at most 6.35 V; M7 with E-F1's capacitor: DC_F moves 2.25 V, so Q1 stands off at most 38.25 V: MEETS (INFERRED)
       the capability scenario (D10 at its rated pulse, not a requirement): negative, Q1 at 100.5 V with DC_P at 36 V, past 100 V by 0.5 V; the
       avalanche energy on the bus behind it at most 83.6 mJ against EAS 274 mJ; the LM74700-Q1's 75 V is passed once DC_P exceeds 10.5 V, and
